Disable libkrun's implicit vsock before adding an explicit one.

smolvm 1.13.1 assumes a libkrun where the implicit vsock is gone -- its own
comment says "the old krun_disable_implicit_vsock is gone". But the libkrun
revision smolvm's flake pins (98163265) still defaults VsockConfig to Implicit,
and its krun_add_vsock returns -EEXIST unless the config is Disabled. Every
boot on the approved pin fails with "krun_add_vsock with TSI failed".

That libkrun does still export krun_disable_implicit_vsock, which sets the
config to Disabled. This patch loads the symbol optionally and calls it before
each krun_add_vsock, so the sequence works on the pinned libkrun and stays
correct on newer revisions where the symbol is absent and there is no implicit
vsock to disable.

Both launchers are patched. launcher.rs drives the boot path that actually
fails; launcher_dynamic.rs carries the same sequence and would fail the same
way.

